  M4 CANDIDATE [D-talk-request ingrid_vik turns=11 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: "You take those walks that don't need to happen. Still breathing your own air?"
    NPC: "Walk my trap line with me? Extra hands, extra eyes."
    YOU: "All right. Let's go."
    NPC: At the trap line the ground is torn up. Something was here, recently, and it wasn't careful. Ingrid's hand finds your sleeve. You leave together, faster than you came.
    YOU: "I'm listening."
    NPC: "We're down to 8 liters of clean water. Haul the creek with me at dawn? Two buckets each, there and back."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "As I said — we're still on that personal stuff."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "We're going in circles — still on that personal stuff. Ask me something else if you want."
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: A beat. Then, as if shaking something off:
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: "...Hi. Sorry. I'm not good at the talking-to-strangers part."
    YOU: "Neither am I, honestly."
    NPC: Something eases in their shoulders. "Oh. Okay. That's... that's fine, then."
    YOU: "Go on. I'm listening."
    NPC: "Strangers are just people you haven't disappointed yet. That's what my mother said. Terrible advice, but it got me through parties."
    YOU: "What do you think it means?"
    YOU: "What do you think is actually going on here?"
    NPC: "I don't need to understand it fully. I need to understand it enough. Enough is achievable."
    YOU: "Take your time. I've got nowhere to be."
    NPC: "Okay. We'll pick this up later."
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: You say nothing. Neither do they, for a while — and it's fine.
    NPC: "...Think about it? I'll be around."
    NPC: They're smiling as you go. "Come back anytime."

