    NPC: "About that question — Did you leave someone behind? ...Sorry. You don't have to answer that."
    YOU: "Yes."
    NPC: Just: "Yeah." A long quiet. "Me too."
    YOU: "I'm listening."
    NPC: They pull back half a step — not leaving, just... further.
    YOU: "I'm listening."
    NPC: "I don't talk about that. Not because it's secret — because saying it out loud makes it real in a way I can't afford yet. Someday. Not today."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Still on who you left behind. Don't waste it."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Like I said — we're still on who you left behind."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "We're going in circles — still on who you left behind. Ask me something else if you want."
    YOU: "I'm listening."
    NPC: "So what's your plan here? Just... get through it?"
    YOU: "One day at a time."
    NPC: "Honest. I can work with honest."
    YOU: "I'm listening."
    NPC: "Mine's simple: learn one useful thing a week. This week it's trapping. A plan's just a direction you argue with."
    YOU: "I'm listening."
    NPC: "Alright. Catch you later."
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: You don't answer. The quiet turns pointed.
    NPC: "Good talk. I feel like I know you a little better now."
    NPC: They nod, already turning away.

